A||N||6||MR2KLR||What suspension does a 88 coupe have?||||5||
Z||000000||MR2KLR||11-15-2001||09:54 PM||||<BR>I am picking up my first non-84 fiero ever in 10 days (  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) it is a '88 Coupe here is my question does the 88 coupe have the suspension of the 88 Formula/ GT or is it the same as 84-87 cars or is it totaly diffrent? I thought the all the 88's where the same, peopple allways talk up the suspension on the Formula's & GT's but Nobody ever talks about the poor little under powered coupe. I just found out last week that the 88 coupe has round trim.<BR>Thanks,<BR>   Tom||||reg||5
Z||000001||Hank is Here||11-15-2001||10:01 PM||||The coupe is the same as the 88 GT and Forumla! There are differences though. No rear sway bar and lighter spring rates.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MR2KLR||11-15-2001||10:26 PM||||Thanks for the info. What ever hapened to the my Black / Blue peral 84 SE? do ya part her out or make her prety?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Thanks,<BR>   Tom||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tom88gt||11-15-2001||10:51 PM||||Hank is right on the money.  Most people know about the missing rear sway bar...but over look the fact that the L-4 88s have lighter springs than the V-6 88s...but the brakes are all the same for the 88s.||||reg||6
Z||000004||Hank is Here||11-15-2001||11:02 PM||||I still have that SE.  I put another motor in it.  however somewhere along the way I screwed up the wiring. Never got it to start.  It is sitting in my storage yard now.  I have to get my CJ7 to run then that is next on tap.  Hopefully I'll got to the coupe over Thanksgiving.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||11-16-2001||12:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tom88gt:<BR><B>Hank is right on the money.  Most people know about the missing rear sway bar...but over look the fact that the L-4 88s have lighter springs than the V-6 88s...but the brakes are all the same for the 88s.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>An FYI for everyone......only the front spring rates are softer ("ARC" vs. "ARD").||||reg||1
